.TH HD-DASHBOARD 8 "October 2026" "hd-dashboard" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-dashboard \- run the hyprdebian dashboard, list and forget its hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-dashboard
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR file ]
.B serve
.br
.B hd-dashboard
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR file ]
.B hosts
.br
.B hd-dashboard
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-database
.IR file ]
.B forget
.I host
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-dashboard
is the hyprdebian dashboard, see
.BR hd-dashboard (7).
.TP
.B serve
Runs the dashboard, as
.B hd-dashboard.service
does, on the address and port in the settings.
It makes the database when it does not exist yet.
.TP
.B hosts
Lists the systems with their level, HyprDebian version and address, and when
they last reported.
.TP
.B forget \fIhost\fR
Removes a system, its token and its history, so that its next report
registers a new token.
.PP
Run
.B hosts
and
.B forget
as root: the database is in
.IR /var/lib/private ,
which only root can open.
They do not make the database; the service makes it on its first start.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\  file
Read the settings from
.I file
in place of
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-database\  file
Use the database
.I file
in place of
.IR /var/lib/hd-dashboard/dashboard.db .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error, such as a setting of the wrong type, a missing
database or an unknown host, 2 on wrong arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The settings, in the key
.BR hd-dashboard .
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-dashboard/defaults.json
The default settings.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hd-dashboard/dashboard.db
The database.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the systems:
.PP
.RS
sudo hd-dashboard hosts
.RE
.PP
Let a reinstalled system register its new token:
.PP
.RS
sudo hd-dashboard forget box
.RE
.PP
Try the dashboard without installing it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
echo '{"hd-dashboard": {"listen": "127.0.0.1", "port": 18080}}' > /tmp/dashboard.json
hd-dashboard \-\-config /tmp/dashboard.json \-\-database /tmp/dashboard.db serve
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-dashboard (7),
.BR hd-config-update (8)
